 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "System",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A disconnectable crimp-style connector: SSH-003T-P0.2-H crimp contacts on the wires go into an SHR receptacle housing, which has housing lances, and the receptacle mates with a BM or SM header on the board. Compact, low-profile design. JST calls it the world's first 1.0 mm pitch crimp-style connector."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Receptacle housing styles",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Each receptacle comes with protrusions (SHR-xxV-S-B) or without (SHR-xxV-S); the protrusions widen the housing by 2.0 mm (B grows from A + 2.0 to A + 4.0). The housing is 2.8 mm across and 5 mm long along the mating axis. The 20-circuit size is made only with protrusions."
  },
  {
